nd the answer can vary across it. State it existentially:\n- **States agree** if some table isomorphism φ carries S₁ onto S₂.\n- **States differ** if none does.\n\nThis is independent of the representative. Decide it without enumerating the automorphisms by testing isomorphism of the combined structure, table plus state set. For parity laws the state set is the check-row space with constants, attached as extra coloured vertices.\n\nAlso report how many isomorphisms carry the states out of the total. Declare up front whether \"same states\" allows value flips per distinction or only renaming.","ttft_ms":25543,"type":"result","duration_ms":41852,"uuid":"379cc95a-cf3c-48da-a3ad-336c1dfb57f8","ttft_stream_ms":1110,"time_to_request_ms":54,"first_content_frame_ms":1111,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
